{
  "texts": [
    {
      "content": "Crown Stalks form clusters of upright, green, segmented structures,\neach topped with a plume of varying color depending on its properties.",
      "left": "205.2px",
      "top": "321.8px",
      "scale": "1.4000000000000004",
      "rotate": "0",
      "fontFamily": "melonfruit",
      "fontSize": "28px",
      "color": "rgb(17, 17, 17)"
    },
    {
      "content": "Their fibrous roots intertwine underground, creating communal networks\nfor nutrient exchange.",
      "left": "205.6px",
      "top": "420.6px",
      "scale": "1.4000000000000004",
      "rotate": "0",
      "fontFamily": "melonfruit",
      "fontSize": "28px",
      "color": "rgb(17, 17, 17)"
    },
    {
      "content": "This colonial habit allows them to overtake entire regions, forming\n“crown forests”across humid plains. When releasing pollen in synchrony,\nthey fill the air with a tinted haze that spreads for kilometers.",
